kindlessNetT -- SEQ 388 R2, the net (Tony, 2026-10-21): a kindless local with no writer the build can see is NOT
JITTABLE -- the action is refused by name and runs interpreted. Nothing in the fleet reaches the net (SEQ 388 R1: every
slotted local has a build-visible writer), so this fixture is the net's only reach.

KN-1 is the control: knC is a kindless local written by `= 2`, a scalar writer, so knCtl compiles (built 1) and knOut
reads 7 on both roads. KN-2 is the net: knLoc is an undeclared name in knRead's body -- a local -- read and never
written. Interpreted, a data-less field prints its own tag (bear-trap 26), so the intended value is `knLoc`. Before the
net the prologue slots knLoc i32 and the compiled print reads that slot as a count.
The interpreted twin is this file with `jitter;` deleted (pop.sh builds it).
